.TH "ROLIA-CLI" "1" "October 2026" "rolia-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rolia-cli \- search, browse, and read manga from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rolia-cli
[\fI\,QUERY\/\fR]
.br
.B rolia-cli
search [\fI\,QUERY\/\fR]
.br
.B rolia-cli
init
.br
.B rolia-cli
browse [\fI\,LIBRARY-DIRECTORY\/\fR]
.br
.B rolia-cli
read \fI\,CHAPTER-DIRECTORY\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rolia-cli
searches manga titles using RoliaScan, lets you select a series and chapter,
and opens chapter pages as a temporary PDF. Chapters can also be saved as
permanent PDFs.
.PP
With no arguments, the program prompts for a manga title. A query searches
for that title directly. An exact, unambiguous title match is selected
automatically; otherwise, matching titles are shown in an interactive menu.
Search queries must contain at least two characters.
.PP
During reading, the chapter menu provides Next, Previous, Select chapter,
Download chapter, and Quit. Temporary files are removed after the PDF viewer
closes.
.PP
The series selector starts with the search query already entered, allowing
results to be narrowed and refined immediately. Type in the chapter selector
to filter by chapter number. Matching text is highlighted in both selectors.
The selectors use the full terminal screen with the prompt at the top, so old
output does not remain above the menu. The initial search prompt is not
cleared, keeping it visible in terminals such as the VS Code integrated
terminal.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search
Search interactively when no query is given, or search for the specified
\fIQUERY\fR.
.TP
.B init
Check dependencies and create the application directories.
.TP
.B browse
List series directories in the optional library directory, or in the default
library if omitted.
.TP
.B read
List supported image pages in the specified chapter directory.
.SH READER CONTROLS
.TP
.B Next
Move to the next chapter in the chapter list and open it.
.TP
.B Previous
Move to the previous chapter in the chapter list and open it.
.TP
.B Select chapter
Choose a chapter from the series chapter list.
.TP
.B Download chapter
Save a permanent PDF of the current chapter under the downloads directory.
.TP
.B Quit
Leave the reader menu.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The program requires a POSIX-compatible shell and the following commands:
.BR curl ,
.BR fzf ,
.BR jq ,
.BR md5sum ,
.BR ffmpeg ,
.BR img2pdf ,
and
.BR lsof .
A PDF viewer and a desktop opener such as
.BR xdg-open
or
.BR gio
are also required. Run
.B rolia-cli init
to check for missing dependencies.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for application data. Defaults to
\fI$HOME/.local/share\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for application configuration. Defaults to
\fI$HOME/.config\fR.
.TP
.B ROLIA_CLI_SOURCE_BASE_URL
Source base URL. Defaults to
.I https://roliascan.com.
.TP
.B ROLIA_CLI_PDF_VIEWER
PDF viewer command used to open temporary chapter PDFs. The command must
accept the PDF path as an argument.
.PP
For compatibility, the program also accepts
.B MAN_CLI_SOURCE_BASE_URL
and
.B MAN_CLI_PDF_VIEWER
when their corresponding
.B ROLIA_CLI_
variables are not set.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rolia-cli/downloads/
Downloaded chapter PDFs.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rolia-cli/library/
Default library directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rolia-cli/
Application configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rolia-cli/cache/
Application cache directory.
.PP
The data and configuration paths use
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
and
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when set. Existing
.I man-cli
data and configuration directories are reused when the corresponding
.I rolia-cli
directories do not exist.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start an interactive search:
.RS
.B rolia-cli
.RE
.PP
Search for a title:
.RS
.B rolia-cli
"wind breaker"
.RE
.PP
Initialize application directories and check dependencies:
.RS
.B rolia-cli init
.RE
